drm/esp32s31: adaptive CPU-vs-PPA dispatch, learned per size bucket from the
actual workload, and an asynchronous PPA path

The port tree is gitignored, so these are the whole modified files rather
than a diff. Copy them back over
linux-71-port/drivers/gpu/drm/espressif/{esp32s31-lcd.c,esp32s31-ppa.c,esp32s31-ppa.h}
before building. CUMULATIVE: supersedes 0036 (and 0035, 0032 for these files).

WHY
The CPU/PPA crossover was a constant (ppa_min_bytes, 128 KB), measured on an
idle desktop and under pointer motion. It is not a constant: under Quake,
forcing the engine at exactly that size cost the compositor 27% MORE CPU,
because the DMA contends with the renderer for PSRAM and the driver waited
for it. Under Doom the same bucket is 30x cheaper on the engine. Which side
of the knee an op falls depends on what the rest of the SoC is doing.

WHAT
esp32s31-lcd.c
  ppa_policy (default 1): per (scaled, ilog2 size) bucket, an EMA (1/8) of
  the CPU time each engine costs - CPU path: the whole op; PPA path: setup +
  spin + wake, with the sleep subtracted - and of wall time. Bootstrap 3 ops
  each, then prefer the cheaper with 15% hysteresis, explore the loser 1 in
  32 (1 in 512 when it is >4x behind), and a latency guard to the CPU when
  the engine's wall time exceeds 4x the CPU's. ppa_policy=0 is the old fixed
  threshold. /sys/module/esp32s31_lcd/parameters/ppa_table shows the learned
  table; writing to it resets.
  The source-row cache flush moved into the engine path: the CPU copy paid
  it for nothing.
  ppa_async (default 1): the commit returns while the engine runs.
esp32s31-ppa.c/.h
  esp32s31_ppa_srm split into start/finish. esp32s31_ppa_scale_rect_async()
  returns with the op in flight; any later lock holder drains it
  (esp32s31_ppa_drain) and esp32s31_ppa_wait_idle() does so explicitly
  before the CPU paints the cursor over the scanout. esp32s31_ppa_last_cost()
  reports CPU and slept nanoseconds of the last op.

MEASURED (fresh boot per arm, 320x200 windowed, speaker sound)
                    fixed        adaptive+async
  Doom timedemo     22.2 fps     23.7 fps      lvdesk 6541 -> 6383 ticks
  Quake demo1       14.8 fps     15.1 fps      lvdesk 2094 -> 2033 ticks
Same-boot Doom sweep: fixed 22.1, adaptive 23.9, adaptive+async 24.5,
fixed+async 22.6. Async takes the PPA op's wall time in the commit from
~6 ms to ~0.3 ms.

CAVEATS
Async: the client may rewrite the source before the engine finishes reading
it (a torn frame, not corruption), and the op holds no fb reference. Fine
for a compositor that owns its dumb buffer; revisit before any other client
uses the path.
